<?php elseif($slug==='review'): ?><section><div class="wrap narrow"><h2>What this local rebuild demonstrates</h2><p>A WordPress/WooCommerce catalogue, editable pages and products, search, quote selection, local enquiry storage, staff status management, CSV export and a local notification catcher.</p><h3>Content to review</h3><ul><li>Clearly labelled sample products demonstrate the interface. No live product export has been supplied.</li><li>Projects, client logos and Insights remain unpublished until approved content is available.</li><li>Ten full service drafts (464–491 words each), nine distinct industry drafts and page-specific FAQ answers are ready for approval. Website notes, detailed RFQ fields and privacy wording remain pending.</li><li>Product Development is included by the requirements document; its detailed scope needs business confirmation.</li><li>Six verified reasons to choose PANDATEC are used. The requested seventh reason is missing.</li></ul><h3>Access still needed</h3><p>Production backup and catalogue export, a clean staging environment, approved email delivery settings, analytics identifiers, hosting performance tests and the production security investigation.</p><h3>Verification and remaining work</h3><p>The local checks cover catalogue routes, search, filters, pagination, enquiry validation, attachment restrictions, duplicate prevention, staff permissions, CSV tools and notification failure recovery. The staff-created sample product demonstrates editing in WordPress.</p><p>Local performance improved after removing unused shop scripts and adding a restricted public-page cache. In the same 1280-pixel unthrottled desktop browser, homepage LCP changed from 2.940 to 0.188 seconds, machinery from 3.628 to 0.188 seconds and a product from 2.612 to 0.160 seconds. The after readings use a warmed server cache; each is a single local observation, not a PageSpeed score or production result. Cold-cache response, field INP, production load and hosting/CDN configuration still need acceptance testing.</p><p>Fresh real browser viewport checks passed at 320, 390, 768 and 1440 pixels across key templates with no horizontal overflow. A 320-pixel attachment selection, preview and local save were exercised with a fictional PNG; its authenticated staff download matched the original file. Physical iOS/Android tests remain outstanding.</p><p>The migration file contains 32 proposed mappings taken from the written brief. It is not the complete 117-category inventory. Public child sitemaps rejected retrieval; an authorised export is required to reconcile 713 versus 1,231 products, map tags and identify exact spam URLs.</p><h3>Current acceptance status</h3><ul><li><strong>Independently tested locally:</strong> draft page structure and word counts, relevant FAQs, catalogue/search/filter/pagination routes, quotation selection and saving, staff editing/status/export, permissions, attachment restrictions, duplicate prevention and local notification recovery.</li><li><strong>Implemented but not yet verified:</strong> full host restore, real catalogue scale, and production sitemap eligibility with genuine imported products.</li><li><strong>Awaiting client content or access:</strong> approval of draft business copy; genuine product export and full old-URL inventory; website notes; Projects, client-logo permissions and Insights; final enquiry/privacy requirements.</li><li><strong>Production-only work outstanding:</strong> compromise investigation, backed-up migration, live delivery, analytics receipt, hosting/cache/security acceptance, physical-device tests and authorised launch.</li></ul><h3>How to review</h3><ol><li>Browse Products & Solutions and try machinery filters.</li><li>Add sample products, change quantities and remove a selection in the quote list.</li><li>Complete Request a Quote with fictional details, preview, then save the local test enquiry.</li><li>Sign into the staff area using the separate local access file. Review the enquiry and email catcher.</li><li>Edit a product in WooCommerce and refresh its public detail page.</li></ol><p><a class="btn" href="<?php echo esc_url(admin_url()); ?>">Open staff login</a></p><p>Detailed requirements, migration, testing, operational and launch notes accompany the project in its docs folder. Local robots directives block indexing. Nothing has been deployed.</p></div></section>
